# ap-tools inputs file (template)
# ============================================================================
# Copy this file to 'inputs.env' in the directory you run ap-tools from (or
# point AP_TOOLS_ENV_FILE=<path> at it), then uncomment and edit the variables
# you want to change. Every value below shows the script default.
#
# Precedence: CLI env  >  inputs.env  >  script defaults
#   sudo VAR=value ./ap-tools ...   always wins over this file, because each
#   line keeps the 'VAR="${VAR:-value}"' form. Keep that form when editing.
#
# The file must NOT be world-writable (ap-tools refuses to source it):
#   chmod 640 inputs.env
# It may contain credentials (SWFS_HARBOR_PASS, DNS_ADMIN_PASSWORD, VELERO_S3_*), so prefer 600.
# ============================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Global
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#DEBUG="${DEBUG:-1}"                                    # Debug mode 1=enabled 0=disabled
#MGMT_IP="${MGMT_IP:-<first IP from 'hostname -I'>}"    # Bind IP address for services
#LB_IP="${LB_IP:-$MGMT_IP}"                             # Ingress VIP (MetalLB pool). Single-node: node IP. Multi-node: a dedicated free L2 IP (LB_VIP is a deprecated alias)
#NTP_SERVERS="${NTP_SERVERS:-}"                         # Space/comma-separated NTP servers; forwarded to rke2_installer.sh on install/join; empty = leave OS default
#COREDNS_HOSTS="${COREDNS_HOSTS:-}"                     # Split-horizon only: in-cluster DNS pins "<fqdn>=<ip>,..." (portal./orchestrator. -> ingress VIP) when LAN DNS points them at a reverse proxy
#BASE_DOMAIN="${BASE_DOMAIN:-edge.lab}"                 # Base domain for environment
#HOST_FQDN="${HOST_FQDN:-$(hostname).$BASE_DOMAIN}"     # Host FQDN (hostnames that are already FQDNs are used as-is)
#SWFS_HARBOR_USER="${SWFS_HARBOR_USER:-admin}"          # Username for Harbor and SeaweedFS basic auth
#SWFS_HARBOR_PASS="${SWFS_HARBOR_PASS:-changeme}"       # Password for Harbor and SeaweedFS basic auth

